# Cypher Box — runtime environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. The actual `.env` is
# git-ignored; only this template lives in source control.
#
# How values get into the app: react-native-config bakes the .env file
# into the native build at compile time. Changes to .env require a
# rebuild (cd ios && pod install + restart Metro is enough on iOS;
# `cd android && ./gradlew clean` on Android).
#
# Per-environment: maintain separate .env files per dev / staging /
# production OAuth clients in Google Cloud Console. CI/CD should set
# these as build-time env vars rather than committing files.

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Drive integration (Android off-device Ark backup)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This is the OAuth 2.0 *Web* client ID from your Google Cloud Console
# project. NOT the Android client ID — the Web one is what
# @react-native-google-signin/google-signin needs to mint ID tokens.
#
# How to obtain:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com → your project
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Google Drive API"
#   3. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials →
#      OAuth client ID → Application type: Web application
#      (also create a separate Android client and drop the resulting
#       google-services.json into android/app/)
#   4. Copy the Web client's "Client ID" — it ends in
#      `.apps.googleusercontent.com`
#
# This value is technically not a secret (Android OAuth uses public
# clients with no client_secret) but we keep it in env to support
# multiple environments and avoid a public-repo leak surface for any
# future GCP web credentials.
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (add future env vars below this line)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
